  "note": "Annual retirement of a third of the councillors of Londonderry Corporation (North two, South three, Waterside one); nominations Friday 5 May, poll Monday 15 May 1939, South Ward count 16 May. No aldermen were due. Only the South Ward was contested (Belfast News-Letter, 6, 16 and 17 May 1939). Described as the retiring Unionist members; the label is the News-Letter's description, not a per-name label. Returned unopposed."
